# Three sources feed one section, and the three things missing from all of them are not a
# ragged edge. They are the tail of a structure, the policy inside a heuristic, and the inside
# of the compiler, and each is missing for a different reason.

title Where a blueprint section 2 gets its facts

size 980 640

box types   40  90 280 110 "the data descriptor" "200 types, 807 fields," "real offsets, per build"
box globals 350  90 280 110 "the globals table" "188 addresses and masks," "including flag values"
box specs   660  90 280 110 "35 contract specs" "prose and pseudocode" "for reading all of it"

box sec2    350 280 280 110 "blueprint section 2" "structures, sizes and" "invariants to build from"

note score  660 280 280 110 "74 per cent of the names" "a blueprint needs are" "published. For the three" "betting on cDAC, 89."

note tail   40 460 280 140 "Not published: the tail." "Vtable slots, optional" "members and the generic" "dictionary sit past the" "fixed header."
note policy 350 460 280 140 "Not published: policy." "gc.cpp budgets, inlining" "decisions and the tier" "promotion thresholds are" "computed, not declared."
note jit    660 460 280 140 "Not published: the JIT." "GenTree, the flow graph" "and the phase list are" "compiler internals and" "never sit in a heap."

arrow types sec2
arrow globals sec2
arrow specs sec2
